cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the fair.md convention, please cite it as below."
title: "fair.md — a portable, human- and machine-readable FAIR manifest"
abstract: >-
  fair.md is a lightweight, human- and machine-readable FAIR manifest placed
  at the root of a repository or website. It declares what data a project holds,
  gives an evidence-backed self-assessment of the project's FAIR posture
  (Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, Reusable), separates openness from FAIR,
  and points to deeper machine-readable affordances such as RO-Crate.
type: software
version: "0.3"
date-released: "2026-07-27"
